{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00AK", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-glue-maps}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-glue-sheaves}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:98d6edf3c7899328e0765170abd57e8cbe0acc0f1617e6a920e148ed6b3feb4e", "source_text": "The functor is fully faithful by\nLemma <REF_0001>\nand essentially surjective (via an explicitly given quasi-inverse functor) by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:43fbba662fa0284d26f37254371b317873a998ee9c4ae0fa8bad2a871e390b47", "unit_id": "tag:00AN:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00AK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$f : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_i : \\mathcal{F}_i \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{G}|_{U_i}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\varphi_{ij}$", "MATH_0008": "$g : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\ng_i : \\mathcal{G}|_{U_i} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}_i\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\varphi_{ij}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d275c33abc0205ec911a73fc4db99970cf5a3712bdc0a1076c17c71c5be8d62d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4df07338544ee883e1f49c4a44534f46083b9fab3a724a4406d3a49952f8df29", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis lemma means that if the sheaf <MATH_0001> was constructed\nfrom the glueing data <MATH_0002>\nand if <MATH_0003> is a sheaf on <MATH_0004>, then a morphism\n<MATH_0005> is given by a collection of\nmorphisms of sheaves\n<MATH_0006>\ncompatible with the glueing maps <MATH_0007>. Similarly,\nto give a morphism of sheaves <MATH_0008>\nis the same as giving a collection of morphisms of sheaves\n<MATH_0009>\ncompatible with the glueing maps <MATH_0010>.\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:339eebdea40ead50d969a4bbf22eeb9746fb4b556401b81fe2a29b1b0b4fe259", "unit_id": "tag:00AK:prose-0003"}
